🚗 Smart Car Parking System using millis() | Day 7 Practice (Tinkercad)

This project is part of my Embedded Systems learning journey (Day 7).
Built and tested using Tinkercad simulation with Arduino UNO.

🔥 Project Overview

A simple Smart Car Parking System that detects parking slot availability using sensors and displays real-time status.
The main focus of this project is using millis() function instead of delay() for non-blocking execution.

💡 Key Features
🚗 Real-time parking slot detection
⚡ Non-blocking timing using millis()
🧠 Efficient multitasking logic
🔧 Sensor-based simulation (IR / Ultrasonic concept)
📊 Slot availability indication using LEDs
🧠 Concepts Learned
Arduino Programming Basics
millis() function (important embedded concept)
Sensor interfacing logic
Real-time system thinking
Tinkercad circuit simulation
⚙️ Why millis()?

Instead of stopping the program using delay(),
millis() allows continuous execution of code.

👉 This makes the system:

Faster
More responsive
Real-time ready

This is how real embedded systems work in industries ⚡

